# `vendor/*.tgz` is the declaration for a third-party archive kept directly under `vendor/`. It
# matches no tracked file today: both `@cosyte/*` siblings are registry devDependencies resolved
# through `pnpm-lock.yaml`, so no `pnpm pack` tarball is vendored. The glob stays as the shape
# `vendor/` has always had rather than being narrowed to one filename, so a rename cannot silently
# escape it, and the declared-binary count pinned in `test/scripts/no-emdash-gate.test.ts` moves
# the moment a file matches it.
# Declaring an archive keeps git from ever treating it as text, and it is the declaration that
# `scripts/check-no-emdash.mjs` partitions on: a DEFLATE stream can hold the em dash's UTF-8
# bytes by coincidence, and there is no edit that removes a byte from someone else's compressed
# stream.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT A SILENCER. The em-dash gate REFUSES any `binary` declaration outside
# `vendor/`, so widening the exclusion means editing that script deliberately rather than
# adding a line here. Tracked FILENAMES are scanned whatever this file says, because a
# declaration about a file's bytes says nothing about its name.
vendor/*.tgz binary

# The pinned FHIR definition packages under `vendor/fhir-packages/` are the same case and get the
# same declaration: published third-party archives this repository consumes as DATA, verified by
# sha256 at run time by the conformance harness. The argument above is what decides it, and it is
# about the ARCHIVE, not about the trust: a DEFLATE stream can carry the em dash's UTF-8 bytes by
# coincidence, and if it did there would be no edit that removes a byte from someone else's
# compressed stream. Measured on the pins committed today, both archives scan clean either way, so
# this declaration buys nothing NOW; it is here so that a future pin bump cannot land the gate in a
# state with no remedy. The `binary` declaration covers CONTENT only: the tracked filenames are
# still scanned, and `scripts/phi-scan.ts` reads these bytes on its own path route regardless.
vendor/fhir-packages/*.tgz binary
